  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maintaining critical, lifesaving &amp; integrated SRH and GBV services within the Ugandan refugee response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This UNFPA project provides critical, and lifesaving integrated sexual and reproductive health (SRH) and gender-based violence (GBV) services, with a particular focus on new refugee arrivals and receiving settlements. This project targets 145,291 affected people, 13,067 men,104,220 women, and 28,004 children including 2,907 Persons with Disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
